.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt OTELAUDITD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm otelauditd
.Nd export audit records as OpenTelemetry log records
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar count
.Op Fl e Ar endpoint
.Op Fl f Ar trail | Fl F Ar flags
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads BSM audit records from its own
.Xr auditpipe 4
clone and sends each one as an OTLP log record to the endpoint
configured in
.Xr otel.conf 5 .
It is normally started by the
.Pa otelauditd
rc.d script; see
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Pp
By default the pipe follows the system audit preselection
.Pq Xr audit_control 5 ,
so
.Nm
exports what
.Xr auditd 8
records.
The pipe queue is raised to its maximum; records the kernel drops
because the queue was full are counted in the cumulative monotonic sum
.Ql otelauditd.drops
.Pq attribute Ql otelauditd.drop.kind Ns = Ns Ql auditpipe ,
exported whenever it grows.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-e endpoint"
.It Fl c Ar count
Exit after
.Ar count
audit records.
By default
.Nm
runs until it receives
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
then flushes pending records and exits.
.Dv SIGHUP
reopens the file of the
.Xr otel.conf 5
file target, which
.Xr newsyslog 8
rotates.
.It Fl e Ar endpoint
Send to
.Ar endpoint
instead of the target resolved from the environment and
.Xr otel.conf 5
.Pq including its file target .
Credentials from the
.Xr otel.conf 5
headers file are not sent to it.
.It Fl f Ar trail
Read a BSM trail file, such as one under
.Pa /var/audit ,
instead of the audit pipe, and stop at its end.
.It Fl F Ar flags
Select records with the audit class
.Ar flags
.Pq for example Dq lo,aa ,
see
.Xr audit_control 5 ,
instead of the system preselection.
.It Fl u Ar user
After opening the audit pipe and reading the configuration and
credentials, switch permanently to
.Ar user ,
before the exporter and its spool
.Pq Pa <spool.directory>/otelauditd.spool , see Xr otel.conf 5
are created.
.El
.Sh LOG RECORDS
Each record becomes one log record whose timestamp is the record time.
The
.Va otelauditd.probe
attribute holds the event name from
.Xr audit_event 5 ,
such as
.Dq AUE_EXECVE ,
and
.Va process.pid
the subject process.
The body is one line with the event name and description, the
subject's
.Va auid ,
.Va euid ,
.Va egid ,
.Va ruid
and
.Va pid ,
the
.Va result ,
and any path, text and exec argument tokens, for example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
AUE_EXECVE execve(2) auid=1001 euid=0 egid=0 ruid=1001 pid=4242
    args="ls -l" path=/bin/ls result=success:0
.Ed
.Pp
Exec environment tokens are never exported.
Records that cannot be parsed are skipped with a warning.
.Pp
The outcome sets the record's severity
.Pq Va severityNumber No and Va severityText :
.Bl -tag -width "ERROR (17)" -compact
.It INFO (9)
a successful event, or a record without a return token;
.It WARN (13)
a failed event;
.It ERROR (17)
a failed event of the login and logout
.Pq Li lo
or authentication and authorization
.Pq Li aa
classes of
.Xr audit_class 5 .
.El
.Pp
The subject also becomes the attributes
.Va process.user.id
.Pq euid ,
.Va process.real_user.id ,
.Va process.group.id
.Pq egid ,
.Va process.real_group.id
and, when set,
.Va user.id
.Pq the audit user ;
the outcome becomes
.Va otelauditd.result
.Pq Li success , failure
and
.Va otelauditd.return
.Pq the return value, or the error number of a failure ;
the first path token becomes
.Va file.path .
The instrumentation scope, and the prefix of the tool's own attributes,
is
.Ql otelauditd
whatever
.Va service.name
.Ev ( OTEL_SERVICE_NAME )
the resource reports.
.Sh SECURITY
The audit pipe is opened and configured as root; its capability rights
are then limited to reading, event notification and the drop counter
ioctl, and the process changes to
.Ar user .
.Nm
does not enter capability mode because its exporter must be able to
connect to the collector again after a failure.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors exit 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr praudit 1 ,
.Xr auditpipe 4 ,
.Xr audit_control 5 ,
.Xr audit_event 5 ,
.Xr otel.conf 5 ,
.Xr auditd 8 ,
.Xr otelconf 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
.Sh CAVEATS
All records are exported with the INFO severity; failed events are
distinguished by the
.Li result=failure
field until the exporter library carries per-record severity and
attributes.
